#: admin/settings-page.php:294
msgid "Because every active tag is registered on every request, each tag costs a little memory and time on every page that is not served from a page cache. WordPress also compares every registered shortcode name each time it processes content, so the cost grows with the number of tags. A few hundred tags are not noticeable; thousands are."
